# SDLPoP for PlayStation Portable (PSP)

Native port of **SDLPoP** (Prince of Persia 1) for the Sony PlayStation Portable and PPSSPP emulator, built using the modern `pspdev` toolchain.

## Features

- **Decoupled 1:1 Integer Overlay**: Pause menus, settings menus, and dialogs render at strict 1:1 integer scale ($320 \times 200$) over a GPU-blended semi-transparent dimmed backdrop. Eliminates all font distortion, blurring, and text shimmering.
- **$2\times$ Integer Status Bar / HUD Split**:
  - Playfield ($192\text{ px}$): Scaled to $256\text{ px}$ ($192 \times 4/3$).
  - Status bar / HUD ($8\text{ px}$): Scaled to $16\text{ px}$ ($8 \times 2$) — an exact $2\times$ integer vertical scale for razor-sharp HP triangles and text messages.
- **Display Modes**:
  - `16:10`: Authentic DOS aspect ratio ($436 \times 272$, 22px symmetrical black pillars).
  - `16:9 Wide`: Full widescreen stretch ($480 \times 272$).
  - `4:3`: Authentic DOS CRT aspect ratio ($362 \times 272$, 59px symmetrical black pillars).
- **On-Demand OGG Streaming**: High-quality authentic DOS music streams on-demand via `stb_vorbis` without startup preloading or memory bloat (~150KB peak RAM vs 20MB).
- **Expanded Memory**: Full 64MB user memory partition unlocked (`MEMSIZE 1` in PRX) with a 51MB+ newlib heap (`PSP_HEAP_SIZE_KB(-2048)`).
- **Audio Clamping & Saturated Mixing**: Eliminates sample overflow clipping and comb-filter phasing on hardware.
- **Ergonomic Handheld Controls**:
  - **D-Pad / Analog Stick**: Movement, Crouch (Down), Jump (Up)
  - **Cross ($\times$) / Square ($\square$)**: Action / Shift (Grab ledge, strike sword, careful walk)
  - **Triangle ($\triangle$) / Circle ($\bigcirc$)**: Jump / Climb
  - **L / R Shoulders**: Action / Shift (easy hold while running)
  - **Start**: Pause Game / In-Game Menu
  - **Select**: Display Time Remaining

## Building

Requires the `pspdev` toolchain (with SDL2, SDL2_image, and CMake).

```bash
./build.sh
```

This compiles `prince.prx`, packages `EBOOT.PBP`, and bundles all required data and INI files into `dist/SDLPoP/`.

## Deployment

```bash
./deploy.sh
```

Automatically deploys to:
1. Local PPSSPP emulator (`~/.config/ppsspp/PSP/GAME/CAT_Homebrew/SDLPoP/` and `~/.config/ppsspp/PSP/GAME/SDLPoP/`)
2. Physical PSP units connected via USB (`/Volumes/NO NAME/...` or network automounts).

